id: pm-5f7ayv
title: Align claim guidance with atomic ownership refusal
description: "Current pm claim --help --explain says non-terminal takeover does not require --force, and Agent Guide repeats the older takeover policy. Current SDK runClaim correctly rejects a different claim principal without force or permits an explicit --if-available skip. Reconcile user and agent guidance with the shipped atomic semantics without weakening ownership."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[3]: agent-ux,documentation,lifecycle
created_at: "2026-10-15T04:39:17.189Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T15:46:13.649Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-15T15:10:37.166Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-15T15:10:37.166Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce explained help and distinct-principal claim behavior; Search all public and generated claim ownership guidance; Preserve atomic test-and-set and non-destructive --if-available semantics; Validate documented examples without invoking an unauthorized real takeover
parent: pm-dj98
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "pm claim --help --explain tip and the Agent Guide Ownership Rules describe the atomic test-and-set: a held item refuses with already_claimed_by, --if-available skips without failing, --force is the coordinated takeover and the terminal-item/stale-lock override. No other public or generated guidance carried the stale wording."
expected_result: "Help and agent documentation describe the current claim, skip and explicitly approved takeover contracts consistently."
actual_result: "Sandbox reproduction: distinct principal refused with already_claimed_by (exit 4) and the three next steps, --if-available returned skipped:true, same-principal re-claim was a no-op, --force recorded claim_takeover; help explain prints the new tip."
