comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T04:39:17.189Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict complete2968-item all-status corpus including2688 closed items, fresh claim/takeover/help search plus open/in-progress lists. Full live closed ownership-guidance and atomic-claim lineage read; no open exact owner for stale explained-help guidance. Current explained help directly reproduces the old no-force sentence. Queued open/unclaimed; no change to already completed claim-safety behavior."
  "2026-10-15T12:29:34.870Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation note (2026-10-15): the pm claim --help --explain tip claimed non-terminal takeover needs no --force; the SDK (runClaim) refuses a different claim principal with already_claimed_by unless --force, and --if-available skips without failing. The tip and the Agent Guide Ownership Rules now describe the atomic test-and-set, the --if-available skip, and --force as the coordinated takeover plus terminal-item/stale-lock override. No other public or generated guidance carried the stale wording (grep over docs, skills, packages, README).\n"
  "2026-10-15T12:30:12.707Z","harness:claude-code","Reproduction (2026-10-15, sandbox tracker, built CLI): claim by principal alpha succeeded; a claim by principal beta refused with already_claimed_by (exit 4) and the three next steps (pm next, --if-available, --force only when coordinated); --if-available returned skipped:true with warning claim_skipped_held_by:alpha; re-claim by alpha was a no-op (changed_field_count 0); a --force takeover in the sandbox recorded claim_takeover:alpha->beta. pm claim --help --explain now prints the atomic test-and-set tip. No real-tracker takeover was invoked.\n"
  "2026-10-15T15:46:13.649Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit): the stale-lock clause is now qualified by policy in both the help tip and the Agent Guide: --force is required to override a stale lock only when governance.force_required_for_stale_lock is enabled (the minimal and custom governance presets can disable it).\n"
